nd a growing preference for convenience and efficiency in financial transactions. The proliferation of smartphones and improved internet connectivity have played crucial roles in facilitating this transition. As a result, more consumers have adopted mobile banking applications, which offer a wide range of services including balance inquiries, fund transfers, bill payments, and more.\n\nConsumer behavior studies within this market have highlighted a trend towards cashless transactions, with mobile applications serving as a pivotal tool in this shift. The convenience of managing finances on-the-go, coupled with enhanced security features, has contributed to the increasing reliance on mobile banking solutions. This trend is indicative of a broader movement towards digitalization in the financial services sector, as consumers seek more streamlined and accessible ways to manage their financial affairs.\n\nThe analysis of the mobile banking market in Poland also underscores the importance of understanding consumer preferences and behaviors. Financial institutions have been prompted to innovate and adapt their services to meet the evolving needs of their customers. This includes the development of user-friendly mobile applications with intuitive interfaces and robust security measures to protect user data.\n\nOverall, the MOBILE BANKING MARKET in Poland from 2017 to 2021 reflects a dynamic and rapidly evolving sector within the financial services industry. The focus on mobile applications and cashless payment systems highlights the growing importance of digital solutions in meeting consumer demands for convenience, efficiency, and security in banking services. As the market continues to evolve, it is expected that mobile banking will play an increasingly central role in the financial lives of consumers in Poland.", "BANKS:", "GUS:GUS, officially known as Główny Urząd Statystyczny, is the Central Statistical Office of Poland. It is responsible for collecting, analyzing, and providing comprehensive statistical data and analysis across various sectors. One of its key roles includes conducting studies and surveys on consumer behavior, with a particular focus on the use of information and communication technologies. This includes detailed research on mobile banking usage in Poland, reflecting the growing importance of digital financial services in the country. GUS plays a crucial role in informing public policy and economic planning by offering insights into technological adoption and consumer trends. Through its extensive data collection and analysis efforts, GUS supports the development of informed strategies and decisions in both the public and private sectors.", "WARD METHOD:The Ward method is a hierarchical clustering technique used in the analysis of mobile banking data in Poland", "UNIWERSYTET EKONOMICZNY W POZNANIU:The University of Economics in Poznań, where quantitative research on consumer payment and purchasing behaviors was conducted", "KATEDRA BADAŃ RYNKU I USŁUG:The Department of Market and Service Research at the University of Economics in Poznań, responsible for conducting the quantitative research", "EXCEL:Excel, a software package used for data analysis in the study", "STATISTICA 13.3 PL:STATISTICA 13.3 PL is an analytical software package designed for data analysis. It is utilized extensively in various studies, providing researchers and analysts with robust tools to process and interpret data effectively. The software is known for its comprehensive suite of features that cater to a wide range of analytical needs, making it a valuable asset in the field of data analysis.", "METODA WARDA:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_6c26fb6d5b3eef17ee2f986644c2b74ab304310855ad0e83eb26809359939659_v2"}